  "body": "## What changed\n- Extracted `mask_center` in `crates/motion/src/machining3d/ladder.rs` and added `MASK_RESIDUE = 1.0`.\n- `ladder` now erodes the unmasked `target` by `r + stock_to_leave` first so only model islands act as walls.\n- `mask_center` intersects `mask.above(z)` with `center.offset(r)` (the swept envelope of `center`) instead of raw `target`.\n- `mask_center` opens the standing region by `MASK_RESIDUE * mask.cell()` using mitered offsets (`offset_sharp`) to drop one-cell lattice residue on walls without rounding grid corners.\n- `mask_center` then intersects `center` with `standing.offset(r)` so only centers whose disc meets standing stock remain.\n- Added `masked_empty` tracking in `ladder` so levels emptied by the mask report nothing left to cut instead of \"too narrow\".\n- Added `crates/motion/tests/pocket3d_mask_edge.rs` and `docs/decisions/1749-mask-edge.md`.\n\n## Cause\nIn `sc_logo.camproj`, `S1 Adaptive rough profile` cleared the stock just outside the part silhouette before `S1 Notch adaptive + terrace finish` ran. The re-machining mask boundary sat on the part edge. Because `ladder` intersected `target` with the mask before eroding by the tool radius, the mask boundary acted as a wall one radius thick and left standing stock at the notch open edges where Setup 2 `Soft jaw (9)` stands. Using `target` instead of `center.offset(r)` in `mask_center` also caused a redundant duplicate op with positive `stock_to_leave` to re-cut corner slivers instead of refusing.\n\n## Tests\n- Pins (`crates/motion/tests/pocket3d_mask_edge.rs`):\n  - `a_masked_pocket_still_clears_the_open_edge_beside_a_wall` — ok\n  - `the_mask_still_keeps_the_cutter_off_cleared_ground` — ok\n  - `filleted_notch_after_outside_profile_clears_open_edge_corner_for_jaws` — ok (100 levels at `stepdown = 0.15`, `shell = true`, R3.125 fillets, 0.254 mm outside-profile mask)\n  - `a_redundant_duplicate_with_stock_to_leave_refuses` — ok\n- Gate and clippy after final edit:\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: passed (`wall 15.9 min, 2 step(s), 0 failed`).\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed (0 warnings).\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test pocket3d_open_side --test remachining --test whole_model_pocket`: `pocket3d_open_side` 7 passed; `remachining` 6 passed; `whole_model_pocket` 5 passed, 1 ignored (heavy lane).\n- Mutations:\n  1. Reverted `ladder.rs` to `upstream/main`: `pocket3d_mask_edge` failed 3 of 4 (`a_masked_pocket_still_clears_the_open_edge_beside_a_wall` left Z 1.000 over `(0.050, 19.950)`; `filleted_notch_after_outside_profile_clears_open_edge_corner_for_jaws` left Z 34.826 over `(0.050, 13.184)`; `a_redundant_duplicate_with_stock_to_leave_refuses` refused the smaller finish collar). Restored: 4 passed.\n  2. Set `MASK_RESIDUE = 0.0`: `remachining::a_redundant_duplicate_refuses_rather_than_cutting_air` failed. Restored: `remachining` 6 passed.\n  3. Intersected mask with `&target` instead of `center.offset(r)` in `mask_center`: `a_redundant_duplicate_with_stock_to_leave_refuses` failed. Restored: 4 passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone (`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty).\n\n## Not exercised\n- Running `camcraft-cli` directly on the private `~/sc-parts/sc_logo.camproj` file was blocked by the headless command allowlist (`permission check failed for unsandboxed \".../target/release/camcraft-cli\"`). That project also hits the separate `HolderProfile::enclose` shank-widening issue (`#2199` / PR `#2179`) on `T31 1/4 3FL`.\n- Full `xtask gate batch` and `xtask gate release` suites did not run here (`xtask gate quick` and the listed `camcraft-app` suites ran).\n\n## Overlaps\n- `crates/motion/src/machining3d/ladder.rs`: **#2149** (`feat(boundaries)!`, already stacked on `#2077`, `conflicts`) and **#2035** (`feat(motion)`, incomplete draft, `conflicts`) also modify `pub(super) fn ladder` on non-overlapping lines (`avoid` keep-outs / `stock` arg vs `mask_center` / `standing`). Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: 3D Pocket and Multi-Axis Rough: a re-machining mask no longer creates a false wall along open notch edges after an outside profile cut, and ignores unreachable corners and wall stock-to-leave collars.\n\nFixes #1749\n",
